    },
    {
      "line": 18,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "scene 027.4 — the celestial storm"
    },
    {
      "line": 20,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "scene meta:"
    },
    {
      "line": 21,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "location: Subterranean Temple / Guardian Chamber"
    },
    {
      "line": 22,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "time: year 17,503 (Immediately following scene 027.3)"
    },
    {
      "line": 23,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "participants: Geralt, Oreck, Applicator, Ušumgallu"
    },
    {
      "line": 24,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "focus: Ušumgallu subjects Geralt to Ethereal visions of corruption and tyranny, which Geralt overcomes by accepting internal doubt and plural accountability."
    },
    {
      "line": 25,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "continuity: Immediately follows scene 027.3"
    },
    {
      "line": 26,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "presentation: cutscene"
    },
    {
      "line": 27,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "cutscene purpose: Test Geralt's moral character against corruption and pass the trial of doubt."
    },
    {
      "line": 29,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Celestial Storm"
    },
    {
      "line": 31,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Phase two began without warning—her form blazing with celestial fury that made the chamber's bioluminescence seem pathetic by comparison."
    },
    {
      "line": 32,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The air itself sang with divine authority, with power that preceded Anunnaki arrival, that spoke to forces which had shaped reality before conscious beings learned to question their place within it."
    },
    {
      "line": 34,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Ušumgallu opened rifts in space—tears in reality's fabric that showed glimpses of Ethereal Realm beyond."
    },
    {
      "line": 35,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Spectral chains lashed outward from those rifts, not binding flesh but grasping for consciousness itself."
    },
    {
      "line": 37,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "One chain caught Geralt—wrapped around awareness rather than body—and suddenly he wasn't in the chamber anymore."
    },
    {
      "line": 39,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He stood in the compound."
    },
    {
      "line": 40,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But different."
    },
    {
      "line": 41,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Wrong."
    },
    {
      "line": 42,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The scarred one—Mika—lay dead at his feet, body bearing wounds he recognized as his own telekinetic signature."
    },
    {
      "line": 43,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The five stood over her corpse, accusing gazes that needed no speech to convey judgment."
    },
    {
      "line": 45,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "This is what power does, a voice whispered—not Ušumgallu, but something deeper, older, speaking truth that cut deeper than any physical weapon."
    },
    {
      "line": 46,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "You will have strength to protect or destroy."
    },
    {
      "line": 47,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "How will you choose when anger overrides conscience?"
    },
    {
      "line": 49,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The vision shattered as Oreck—recovered enough to move—grabbed the spectral chain and tore it free with claws that left furrows in ethereal matter."
    },
    {
      "line": 51,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "\"Illusion!\""
    },
    {
      "line": 52,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "the reptilian shouted. \"Don't believe what she shows you!\""
    },
    {
      "line": 54,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But more chains emerged."
    },
    {
      "line": 55,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Dozens."
    },
    {
      "line": 56,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Hundreds."
    },
    {
      "line": 57,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Each carrying different vision, different possibility, different future where power corrupted and good intentions paved roads to atrocity."
    },
    {
      "line": 59,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt saw himself as tyrant."
    },
    {
      "line": 60,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "As liberator turned oppressor."
    },
    {
      "line": 61,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "As hero becoming villain through incremental choices that seemed justified in moments but accumulated into horror."
    },
    {
      "line": 63,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Is this what you want?"
    },
    {
      "line": 64,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The voice pressed."
    },
    {
      "line": 65,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "To trade Anunnaki chains for your own?"
    },
    {
      "line": 66,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "To free slaves only to enslave them to your will?"
    },
    {
      "line": 68,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "\"NO!\""
    },
    {
      "line": 69,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt screamed—not at the illusions but at himself, at the fear that perhaps the visions carried truth, that perhaps claiming godlike power would inevitably corrupt despite intentions."
    },
    {
      "line": 71,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Memory flashed—the Applicator's invasion."
    },
    {
      "line": 72,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Puppeting the five."
    },
    {
      "line": 73,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Feeling their consciousness subordinate to his will."
    },
    {
      "line": 74,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The seductive ease of absolute control."
    },
    {
      "line": 76,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He'd hated it."
    },
    {
      "line": 77,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Hated how natural it felt."
    },
    {
      "line": 78,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Hated that part of him had enjoyed certainty that came with unquestioned authority."
    },
    {
      "line": 80,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "\"I'm not...\""
    },
    {
      "line": 81,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "he struggled to articulate through visions battering consciousness, \"...I'm not claiming power for myself. I'm becoming weapon. Tool. Instrument that others can check, can question, can hold accountable.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 83,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The chains paused—spectral links hovering as though considering his words."
    },
    {
      "line": 85,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Geralt",
      "text": "\"The armor,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 87,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "\"I'll be plural. Contested. Accountable not through external authority but through internal disagreement.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 89,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The chains withdrew slightly—not released but reconsidering, reassessing whether this mortal understood what he was claiming, what burden plural consciousness carried."
    },
    {
      "line": 91,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "\"You speak wisdom,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 92,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Ušumgallu said, voice carrying less certainty, more genuine curiosity. \"But speaking and living are different things. The armor will amplify everything you are—nobility and darkness equally. Can you accept that becoming weapon means becoming capable of atrocity?\""
    },
    {
      "line": 94,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Geralt",
      "text": "\"I already am capable of atrocity,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 96,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He met the dragon's six eyes directly."
    },
    {
      "line": 98,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "\"I can't promise I'll never abuse power. Can't guarantee I'll always choose correctly. But I can promise I'll never stop questioning myself. Never stop listening to voices that challenge me. Never become so certain of righteousness that I stop doubting my choices.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 100,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Silence filled the chamber—not empty but pregnant with decision being weighed, with future being determined through conversation rather than combat."
    },
    {
      "line": 102,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Then Ušumgallu laughed—genuine sound that carried relief and sorrow and recognition that this mortal, at least, understood what divine power truly cost."
    },
    {
      "line": 104,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "\"Phase two complete. The trial of doubt. You acknowledge darkness within. Accept plurality rather than certainty. Perhaps...\""
    },
    {
      "line": 106,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Her coils relaxed further, and the chamber's atmosphere shifted—less trial ground, more meeting space."
    },
    {
      "line": 108,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "\"One phase remains. The hardest. The one that determines whether you claim armor or die attempting.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 110,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Her body began to glow—not with divine authority but with something approaching vulnerability, approaching hope that perhaps, perhaps, these mortals could offer what epochs of isolation had denied."
    },
    {
      "line": 112,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "she",
      "text": "\"Free me,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 114,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "\"And in exchange, I grant you passage to what you seek.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 116,
      "type": "scene_header",
      "text": "---"
    }
  ],
